; SKULL.SCR — Order of the Skull guild area (org 28)
; Source: "LoFP Order of the Skull material.pdf" GM planning doc.
; Scope of this pass: organization + rooms only. Spell additions (327-399) from
; the source material are deliberately NOT implemented here. Tower/inner-tower
; entry is gated by simple ORG membership (matching ARCANA.SCR's org-2 "unseen
; force" idiom) rather than the source doc's full robe+passphrase ritual, since
; that needs a robe item that doesn't exist yet. The throne/onyx-skull secret
; passage to the Skull Lord's chamber IS implemented as a real hidden puzzle
; (see room 5302), following the look-behind/reveal idiom from ADDAMS.SCR room
; 3714's painting-safe.
;
; Rooms:
;   5300  Graveyard, Tower            (cul-de-sac; reached via room 307's path)
;   5301  Order of the Skull, Foyer
;   5302  Great Hall of the Skull
;   5303  Chamber of Necrology        (skill training)
;   5304  Anatomicatory               (reagent shop)
;   5305  Chamber of the Skull Lord   (leader's private chamber; markable)
;
; New vocabulary added to ADJNOUN.SCR: NOUNDEF 1598 engraving.

ORGDEF 28 INVITE GUILD 5301 Order_of_the_Skull

VARIABLE SKULLOPEN

; ── Item archetypes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

; Path up from the cemetery (room 307) — unrestricted; anyone can walk up and
; look at the tower from outside. Placed as a room item in both 307 (in
; FAYD.SCR) and 5300 below, each pointing at the other.
INUMBER 8300
NAME 154
MISC
WEIGHT 1000
VOLUME 1000
PORTAL_CLIMB
;
; A weathered bone skull set into the tower's base, below the engraving.
; EXAMINE text for this is set per-room (room-scoped *DESCRIPTION_START ITEM
; EXAMINE <idx> — archetype-level item descriptions only apply when carried).
INUMBER 8301
NAME 188
ADJ1 31
MISC
WEIGHT 5
VOLUME 2
FIXED
;
; The engraving above the skull.
INUMBER 8302
NAME 1598
MISC
WEIGHT 1
VOLUME 1
FIXED
IFPREVERB READ -1
  CLEARVERB
  ECHO PLAYER There is a burst of sickly green eldritch light from the engraving that highlights the words, 'Order of the Skull'.
  ECHO OTHERS %N reads an engraving, which flashes with sickly green eldritch light.
ENDIF
;
; The teeth — the actual entrance into the tower. Org-gated; blocked players
; get pushed back rather than let inside.
INUMBER 8303
NAME 281
MISC
WEIGHT 1000
VOLUME 1000
PORTAL_CLIMB
HIDDEN
IFPREVERB GO -1
  IFVAR ORG ! 28
    CLEARVERB
    ECHO PLAYER As you attempt to climb between the teeth, a terrible scream assaults your ears and you are thrown forcibly back and knocked to the ground!
    ECHO OTHERS %N attempts to climb into the tower's mouth but is thrown back with a terrible scream and knocked to the ground!
    POSITION LAY
  ENDIF
ENDIF
;
; Bone archway inside the foyer, leading deeper into the tower. Unrestricted —
; anyone who made it through the teeth is already a member.
INUMBER 8304
NAME 7
ADJ1 31
MISC
WEIGHT 1000
VOLUME 1000
PORTAL_THROUGH
HIDDEN
;
; The bone throne at the north end of the Great Hall. EXAMINE/BEHIND text for
; this is set per-room below (room 5302), same reasoning as the bone skull.
INUMBER 8305
NAME 478
ADJ1 31
MISC
WEIGHT 1000
VOLUME 1000
FIXED
HIDDEN
;
; The onyx skull hidden behind the throne — concentrate/pull/tap/push all
; trigger the same reveal, opening the way to the Skull Lord's chamber.
INUMBER 8306
NAME 188
ADJ1 224
MISC
WEIGHT 50
VOLUME 5
SUBSTANCE HARDSTONE
FIXED
HIDDEN
IFPREVERB CONCENTRATE -1
  IFVAR SKULLOPEN = 1
    CLEARVERB
    ECHO PLAYER Nothing happens — the passage is already open.
  ELSE
    CLEARVERB
    EQUAL SKULLOPEN 1
    ECHO PLAYER A section of the wall slides to your left, revealing a spiraling stairway leading upward into darkness.
    ECHO OTHERS A section of wall slides open behind the throne, revealing a hidden stairway.
  ENDIF
ENDIF
IFPREVERB PULL -1
  IFVAR SKULLOPEN = 1
    CLEARVERB
    ECHO PLAYER Nothing happens — the passage is already open.
  ELSE
    CLEARVERB
    EQUAL SKULLOPEN 1
    ECHO PLAYER A section of the wall slides to your left, revealing a spiraling stairway leading upward into darkness.
    ECHO OTHERS A section of wall slides open behind the throne, revealing a hidden stairway.
  ENDIF
ENDIF
IFPREVERB TAP -1
  IFVAR SKULLOPEN = 1
    CLEARVERB
    ECHO PLAYER Nothing happens — the passage is already open.
  ELSE
    CLEARVERB
    EQUAL SKULLOPEN 1
    ECHO PLAYER A section of the wall slides to your left, revealing a spiraling stairway leading upward into darkness.
    ECHO OTHERS A section of wall slides open behind the throne, revealing a hidden stairway.
  ENDIF
ENDIF
IFPREVERB PUSH -1
  IFVAR SKULLOPEN = 1
    CLEARVERB
    ECHO PLAYER Nothing happens — the passage is already open.
  ELSE
    CLEARVERB
    EQUAL SKULLOPEN 1
    ECHO PLAYER A section of the wall slides to your left, revealing a spiraling stairway leading upward into darkness.
    ECHO OTHERS A section of wall slides open behind the throne, revealing a hidden stairway.
  ENDIF
ENDIF
;
; The spiral stairway revealed behind the throne. Climbing it before the wall
; has been opened just finds bare stone.
INUMBER 8307
NAME 193
ADJ1 306
MISC
WEIGHT 1000
VOLUME 1000
PORTAL_CLIMBUP
HIDDEN
IFPREVERB GO -1
  IFVAR SKULLOPEN ! 1
    CLEARVERB
    ECHO PLAYER You don't see any stairway here.
  ENDIF
ENDIF
;
; Informational skull in the Anatomicatory, listing shop prices on LISTEN.
INUMBER 8308
NAME 188
MISC
WEIGHT 5
VOLUME 2
FIXED
HIDDEN
IFPREVERB LISTEN -1
  CLEARVERB
  ECHO PLAYER The skull whispers, "The Order sells the following components:"
  ECHO PLAYER Wight dust - 5 crowns, Mandrake root - 90 crowns, Nightshade - 7 crowns,
  ECHO PLAYER Stalker eyes - 100 crowns, Stalker lips - 250 crowns,
  ECHO PLAYER Stalker tongues - 50 crowns, Zovembie fingers - 5 crowns,
  ECHO PLAYER Babich root - 1 crown.
ENDIF

; ── Rooms ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

NUMBER 5300
NAME Graveyard, Tower
OUTDOOR_FLOOR
DAY_LIGHT
*DESCRIPTION_START
As the gravestones fall below and behind you along the path, the ebon tower
looms before you, cold and ominous in the light. It resembles a giant skull
composed of black bone that faces south, the upper floor windows resembling
dark eyesockets that stare out over the graveyard. The jaw, mouth, and two
thick vertebrae form the lower section of the tower. Pale ivory teeth, that
sit over a man's height above the ground, make you feel a little like food
where you stand. The withered undergrowth intertwines thickly to either side
of the tower, forming a natural cul-de-sac.
*DESCRIPTION_END
ITEM 0 8300 VAL2=307
ITEM 1 8301
ITEM 2 8302
ITEM 3 8303 VAL2=5301
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAMINE 1
A normal sized skull of bone rests below an engraving on the front of the
tower that gives a name to the dark imposing face that fills you with
trepidation.
*DESCRIPTION_END
;
NUMBER 5301
NAME Order of the Skull, Foyer
INDOOR_FLOOR
FIXED_LIGHT
*DESCRIPTION_START
Flaming skulls, two on each of the side walls just below the arched ceiling,
bathe this small room dimly in an eerie flickering light. The ceiling is
supported by a bone pillar in the corners of this chamber, while the ceiling
arches to a point supported by four curved bone buttresses which rest on the
pillars and meet at the apex of the ceiling. An ornate bench rests against
the right wall, while a narrow bone table sits against the left, their pale
bone surfaces dully reflecting the firelight. The teeth through which you
entered the tower form the curved south wall of this room, sealing it
tightly from the outside. A bone arch opposite the teeth leads deeper into
the tower.
*DESCRIPTION_END
; arch
ITEM 0 8304 VAL2=5302
; teeth
ITEM 1 8303 VAL2=5300
;
NUMBER 5302
NAME Great Hall of the Skull
INDOOR_FLOOR
FIXED_LIGHT
*DESCRIPTION_START
Your footsteps echo on the stone of this great hall as your eyes are drawn to
the center of the room where the image of a skull is suspended in the floor
within a circle of pure black obsidian that is edged with white gold. Six
pillars of ornately carved onyx, two white, two grey, and two black, run
south to north and form a natural aisleway towards an enormous throne of
bone that rests upon three pyramidal stone steps at the north end of the
hall. Two spectral warriors stand at attention next to the throne, one on
either side. Three flaming skulls sit high up on the east and west walls,
illuminating rows of high-backed chairs of bone as well as small bone tables
that sit next to each chair along both walls, on the outside of the
aisleway. Archways of bone on the side walls lead to other chambers.
*DESCRIPTION_END
EXIT E 5304
EXIT W 5303
ITEM 0 8305
ITEM 1 8306
ITEM 2 8307 VAL2=5305
; arch
ITEM 3 8304 VAL2=5301
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAMINE 0
An enormous throne of bone rests upon three pyramidal stone steps. Power
seems to linger in the air around it.
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM BEHIND 0
You walk up close to the throne and look behind it. You see an onyx skull
set into the wall.
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAMINE 1
The skull looks to be composed of bluish-grey shards along with flecks that
have been infused into the wall. It stares back at you from the stone.
*DESCRIPTION_END
;
NUMBER 5303
NAME Chamber of Necrology
INDOOR_FLOOR
FIXED_LIGHT
*DESCRIPTION_START
Bookshelves and slateboards made of bone line the walls of this room, the
largest slateboard located on the west wall, opposite the arch. A podium and
a desk, also made of bone, stand in front of the board. Granite alchemical
tables and glass laboratory apparati fill the north side of this room, while
tomes and other books on the south side provide reference material to Order
members seeking knowledge. Bone tables and chairs set to face the podium
form a rough semicircle in the center of the room, now sparsely occupied by
figures involved in study. The students, whose robes display low flames, are
attended by a silent hooded figure who quickly fetches tomes when called
upon. An older instructor, wearing a robe whose flames reach to his waist,
tutors fledgling students in the magical arts at a table near the center of
the room.
*DESCRIPTION_END
EXIT O 5302
TRAINING 5 5
TRAINING 11 10
TRAINING 10 15
TRAINING 14 20
TRAINING 23 50
TRAINING 29 50
TRAINING 30 90
TRAINING 32 10
;
NUMBER 5304
NAME Anatomicatory
INDOOR_FLOOR
FIXED_LIGHT
*DESCRIPTION_START
Examination tables lie within this stark chamber, under floating orbs of
bright light. A small number of students lean over the dissection of a
cadaver in the northern section of this room, while a man with a robe
displaying high flames explains differences in humanoid anatomy to those
assembled. Diagrams illustrating the various techniques for identifying
undead adorn the walls of this area, near the form of a ghoul that has been
stuffed and posed in a position of attack. Shelves filled with plant and
animal parts cover the south wall of this chamber, many of the jars holding
parts suspended in an amber preservative liquid. A small spectacled man in
flaming robes oversees the categorizing and storage of new parts brought by
younger members, as well as manages the sale of such items to those in need
of the rare components. A skull on the wall over the man's shoulder whispers
information concerning the prices of this shop.
*DESCRIPTION_END
EXIT O 5302
