NUMBER 5305
NAME Chamber of the Skull Lord
INDOOR_FLOOR
FIXED_LIGHT
*DESCRIPTION_START
This richly furnished octagonal room is warmer and more well lit than the
rest of the tower. Against the east wall rests a large bone canopy bed that
is draped and covered in black silk embroidered with silky red and yellow
flames. In the center of the room is an enormous circular rug vividly
depicting a necromancer leading an army composed of all types of undead. A
large stately desk of carved bone lies against the south wall between two
round red leaded crystal windows. A huge ornate chandelier composed of
various bones ending in nine flaming skulls hangs from the center of the
domed ceiling, providing warmth and light. Flaming skulls on the walls flank
both the desk and the bed. A large tapestry of a tall, ominous man in flaming
robes commanding undead to rise from the soil hangs from the west wall. The
window looks out over the graveyard past the mausoleums and markers to the
south of the city; the poorer section of the city is visible off to the
left, while the Eltimar and the forest of Grymwood stretches to the right,
and the shores of the inner sea are just visible over a range of low hills.
*DESCRIPTION_END
ITEM 0 81 VAL2=5302 ; STAIRS

